t.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b26\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"There is no case at all where a guess is the better of the two.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a25, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a26\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"2. Retry only what is safe to retry — a smaller set than everything that isn't a success.\", \"reason\": \"Combined with b27's smaller-set clarification.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b27\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"2. Retry only what is safe to retry — a smaller set than everything that isn't a success.\", \"reason\": \"Its clarification joined into a26's rule heading.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b28\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"A 200 wants nothing, a 429 wants the stated wait, a 500 may be retried once that wait has passed, and a 503 is the overload path.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a27, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b29\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"A client that folds every non-success into one branch will retry hardest during exactly the incident the cap was installed to survive.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a29, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b30\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"Avoid writing that loop.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a30, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a32\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as b31, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b31\", \"disposition\": \"superseded\", \"replacement\": \"A batch credential is allowed fifty times the default allowance, and it is measured over exactly the same window.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a32, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b32\", \"disposition\": \"reworded\", \"replacement\": \"The window, the header and the body are identical to the interactive case, so a client written for one tier needs no change to run against the other.\", \"reason\": \"Unique detail carried in condensed form.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b33\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"Nothing else about the two tiers differs in any way.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a34, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a35\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"4. Log every refusal seen, and keep the log for at least a week.\", \"reason\": \"Combined with b34's keep-for-a-week detail.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b34\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"4. Log every refusal seen, and keep the log for at least a week.\", \"reason\": \"Its retention detail joined with a35's rule heading.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b35\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"A caller that cannot say how often it was refused last week cannot argue for a larger cap, and nobody at the far end will assemble that argument on its behalf.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a36, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b36\", \"disposition\": \"reworded\", \"replacement\": \"The counts are the whole of the argument — without them a request is only a preference.\", \"reason\": \"Unique closing point on rule 4 carried as new sentence.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b37\", \"disposition\": \"superseded\", \"replacement\": \"## Other refusals and their codes\", \"reason\": \"Base heading chosen instead.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b38\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"The gateway refuses a request for three reasons and only one of them is the one above\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a39/a40, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b39\", \"disposition\": \"reworded\", \"replacement\": \"two of the three have nothing to do with how much traffic a caller has sent in the window it is currently in\", \"reason\": \"Unique elaboration carried as added clause.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a41\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit and be refused before it has even been read.\", \"reason\": \"Combined with b40's before-it-is-read detail.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b40\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"A credential may be suspended, a route may be closed for maintenance, or a body may exceed the 5 megabyte limit and be refused before it has even been read.\", \"reason\": \"Its extra detail joined with a41's list of reasons.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b41\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"The distinction matters to a retry loop.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a43, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b42\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"A loop that waits and retries against a suspended credential spends its whole budget without ever reaching the service\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a44, restated in combined sentence.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a44\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals and no successes — which reads like an outage and isn't one, and the wasted budget is the caller's own\", \"reason\": \"Combined with b43's outage-framing and cost detail.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b43\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"the log afterwards shows nothing at all except a long run of refusals and no successes — which reads like an outage and isn't one, and the wasted budget is the caller's own\", \"reason\": \"Its framing joined with a44's description.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a47\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"A cap can be raised, and the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0 — an assertion that the current one is too small is not enough on its own.\", \"reason\": \"Combined with b46's assertion-not-enough clause.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b46\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"A cap can be raised, and the number of caps raised without a measurement behind them is 0 — an assertion that the current one is too small is not enough on its own.\", \"reason\": \"Its clause joined with a47's numeric fact.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b47\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"Bring a week of refusal counts, the shape of the traffic across the day, and the deadline that traffic is serving.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a48, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a49\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"The platform team wants to know whether the load is smooth or bursty before it looks at the number at all, because a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\", \"reason\": \"Combined with b48's before-the-number detail.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b48\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"The platform team wants to know whether the load is smooth or bursty before it looks at the number at all, because a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak.\", \"reason\": \"Its ordering detail joined with a49's statement.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b49\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"a burst is cheaper to smooth than it is to serve at its peak\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a49, restated in combined sentence.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b44\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually finds it doesn't need a larger cap in the first place\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a50, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a50\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually finds it doesn't need a larger cap in the first place — the cheapest fix available to anybody, and one available to almost everybody.\", \"reason\": \"Combined with b45's cheapest-fix framing.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b45\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"A caller that can move half its work to a quieter hour usually finds it doesn't need a larger cap in the first place — the cheapest fix available to anybody, and one available to almost everybody.\", \"reason\": \"Its framing joined with a50's outcome.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b50\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a51, a's wording kept.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"a51\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel, and they are answered within two working days; chasing the answer doesn't make it come any faster.\", \"reason\": \"Combined with b52's chasing-doesn't-help detail.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b52\", \"disposition\": \"reconciled\", \"replacement\": \"Requests reach the platform team through the usual channel, and they are answered within two working days; chasing the answer doesn't make it come any faster.\", \"reason\": \"Its added detail joined with a51's turnaround statement.\"},\n    {\"segment\": \"b51\", \"disposition\": \"duplicate\", \"replacement\": \"There is no expedited path and no exception list.\", \"reason\": \"Same fact as a52, a's wording kept.\"}\n  ],\n  \"mismatch\": \"\"\n}","ttft_ms":85243,"type":"result","duration_ms":134251,"uuid":"426d1e69-b020-4cd9-a1c8-554c0e1db771","ttft_stream_ms":1594,"time_to_request_ms":60,"first_content_frame_ms":1594,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
